[32m+[m[32m## 22. Permanent page-responsibility hierarchy (approved 2026-09-20)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Overview -> Domain page -> Record / Asset page** is the permanent Plant design principle.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Overview:** organisation-level summary, exceptions, financial pressure and navigation. It aggregates trustworthy loaded information and routes management to action.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Domain page:** the detailed control workspace for one Plant domain, with its own queue, filters and workflow controls.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Record / Asset page:** full information, authorised actions and editing, evidence and history for one record or asset.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe detailed capabilities listed earlier in this document are domain targets, not an instruction to reproduce them all on Overview. A summary cannot replace a canonical workflow. Assigned does not mean physically deployed. Missing evidence never establishes safety, readiness or compliance.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Page responsibility contract[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Page | Primary management question | Information shown | Intended authorised actions | Intentionally not shown | Relationship to Overview and drill-down |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| Overview | What requires management attention across Plant? | Aggregate position, asset-centred exceptions, known financial pressure, project grouping and upcoming events | Filter/toggle loaded summaries, expand concerns, open the relevant working workspace, refresh | Full asset records, certificate matrices, detailed repair/service histories, duplicate data-entry workflows | Entry point: summary -> domain filtered to the concern -> record/asset -> action -> return and refresh |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Fleet | What assets do we have and what is their current recorded position? | Searchable portfolio, ownership, type, state, assignment/location, explicit restrictions and authorised hire position | Create assets through the existing workflow, filter/search, open Asset; authorised edits through Asset | Full evidence matrices, complete event histories or an organisation action dashboard repeated inside the register | Overview position -> Fleet filter -> Asset -> update -> return |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Requests | What Plant demand needs clarification, sourcing or fulfilment? | Demand, requester/project, required capability, dates, priority, fulfilment and linked records | Raise, clarify, source, approve/reject where authorised, partially fulfil and link to the established asset/assignment/movement lifecycle | Duplicate Fleet creation, fabricated stock/availability or replacement financial ledgers | Overview demand exception -> request queue -> request record -> fulfilment -> linked asset/workflow |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Availability | What can be allocated, when, and what blocks its use? | Recorded operational restrictions, current/future assignments, overlapping commitments, idle position, location confidence and authorised hire implications | Filter by need/date/project, inspect conflicts, route to authorised assignment, release or movement actions | Unsupported ready/safe conclusions, physical deployment inferred from assignment, detailed repair histories | Overview available/idle/conflict -> Availability -> commitment/Asset -> resolve through the owning workflow |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Movements | What must move, when, and what is preventing collection or delivery? | Planned/booked/in-transit movements, route/access controls, collection/delivery dates, owners and recorded completion | Plan/book transport, update progress, confirm collection/delivery with history and evidence where required | Assignment treated as proof of delivery, detailed defect/compliance histories, unauthorised transport costs | Overview upcoming/transport exception -> Movements filter -> movement record -> update -> Asset location/history |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Defects | What Plant is defective/restricted, what is the repair position, and what action is required? | Open faults, recorded severity/isolation, engineer/parts position, responsible person, repair milestone and authorised costs | Triage, assign repair, update diagnosis/parts/progress, record evidence and route to authorised return-to-service | Automatically removing restrictions on closure, maintenance history unrelated to the fault, full portfolio duplication | Overview restriction -> Defects queue -> defect record/Asset -> repair and authorised return-to-service |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Maintenance | What servicing is required, planned, overdue or completed? | Established service baseline, meter/interval evidence, due dates, bookings, owners and completion position | Establish/update an authorised schedule, plan/book service, record completion and evidence, apply authorised state transitions | Treating absent schedules as no maintenance due, unrelated defect histories or compliance certification | Overview due-service exception -> Maintenance queue -> service record/Asset -> complete and verify |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Compliance | Can each asset legally/operationally remain in service, and what evidence supports that position? | Requirement/applicability and certificate/evidence matrix, assessments, explicit holds, verified dates and evidence gaps | Review requirements/evidence, route uploads through controlled Documents, record authorised assessments and hold decisions | Compliance inferred from missing records, a duplicate binary document store, invented expiry or legal conclusions | Overview count/status/explicit hold only -> Compliance matrix -> requirement/evidence/Asset -> assess and act |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Suppliers | Who can supply, repair or transport Plant, and how do we contact them? | Supplier identity, services, contacts, active status and linked records; authorised financial data only | Maintain supplier details, select for owning workflows, inspect linked activity | Unsupported performance scores, a duplicate hire ledger, confidential prices for restricted roles | Overview supplier-related concern -> relevant domain record -> supplier details and linked activity |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Asset | What is the complete current truth and history of this machine? | Permanent identity, assignment/location history, hire periods, defects, maintenance, inspections, evidence, issues and authorised costs | Authorised editing and lifecycle actions, evidence access, location confirmation, linked assignment/movement/repair/off-hire workflows | Organisation-wide dashboards, duplicate canonical event records, manual inspection creation outside its owning workflow | Domain record -> Asset -> act on the owning record -> retain history -> return to domain/Overview |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThese are intended responsibilities, not claims that every page or action is implemented. Scope and permissions must be checked before each workflow is built. The Compliance matrix belongs to Compliance; Overview currently consumes explicit holds only and does not derive certificate expiry.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Bounded Overview interaction and attention contract[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Fleet Position segment and legend clicks use the same toggle: select a category, click again for All Fleet, or select another category. Visually and accessibly identify the selected category. Filter existing lower tables; never create a duplicate asset section.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Attention is one expandable management row per identified asset. Summarise overall urgency, primary issue, known impact, active concern count and next action. Retain unrelated/unlinked concerns separately rather than merging them into a fictitious asset.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Expanded content shows individual concerns, recorded context/dates and actions with one asset identity. Preserve known blockers when another source fails.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Blue means confirmation/data action. Amber means approaching/due soon. Dark amber means present commercial/operational pressure. Red requires an explicit restriction or supported material impact; uncertainty alone is never red.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Combined overdue active hire, established non-assignment and missing location confirmation may justify red commercial-control urgency only with a known positive current commitment. This is not a statement of proven financial loss.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Rank by known urgency, then known weekly commitment where cost access permits. Do not invent savings, lost production, avoidable-cost history or idle durations.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Overdue off-hire financial emphasis means **current weekly commitment on hires past expected off-hire**. It is not a new estimate of charges since the planning date. Canonical hire calculations remain unchanged. Withhold totals when required inputs are incomplete or unknown.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Operational Control Review must use a real domain page when implemented. Until then, use a clearly bounded expansion/filter of loaded Overview records or label the action unavailable. Never link to an empty page as though a workflow exists.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAfter these refinements, stop Overview iteration and prioritise detailed domain work. Fleet is the recommended next workspace: it is the existing creation/register route and provides the asset identity and drill-down foundation used by the remaining domains. Security-sensitive writes retain their release gates.[m
